<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xri version="1.0">
   <description>
      <h2>Stirling Astrophoto PixInsight Repository for AnnotateImageExt</h2>
   </description>
   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.9.4.1695:1.9.9">
      <package fileName="2026-08-23-AnnotateImageExt.tar.gz" sha1="36245ca6bc06557ee3e04d7f307a24bdadcd3992" type="script" releaseDate="20260823">
         <title>AnnotateImageExt, install / update</title>
         <description>
            <p>v1.4</p>
            <ul>
               <li>SGA 2020 VizierCatalog added, update to and subset of PGC, with common names, D26 diameters, axisRatio, PA (and work in progress: r_mag_SB24 filter). Update updates.xri from last release.</li>
               <li>Add UCAC5 and replace UCAC3, outdated.  Even UCAC5 is based on Gaia DR1, which is older (Gaia DR3 is latest).</li>
               <li>Fix CMC-14 broken catalog in PixInsight 1.9.x due to incorrect coordinate column names in the Vizier query, test, then update to CMC-15 and test and fix another change in the coordinate column names there.</li>
               <li>Update Milliquas from v7.2 -&gt; v8 and Guide Star Catalog (GSC) from v2.3 to vx2.4.2</li>
               <li>Add documentation for VizierCache and AnnotateImage Preview: Document the functionality and usage of VizierCache in AnnotateImage, including its role in caching query results and the implications for the Preview feature.</li>
               <li>Replace banner image in README: Updated image in README and modified dimensions.</li>
               <li>Update version from 1.3 to 1.4</li>
               <li>Update README with new fixes, catalogs and documentation.</li>
               <li>Add first pass at documentation of the catalogs-config.json for AnnotateImageExt.</li>
               <li>Reorder catalogs listing a bit to be more categorized and listed historically and/or alphabetically. Added a few details and tweaks to names and descriptions to normalize them.</li>
               <li>Remove and comment out TODOs and DEBUG statements</li>
            </ul>
            <p>v1.3</p>
            <ul>
               <li>Update updates.xri for next release and fix CatalogDownloader problem, https://github.com/scottstirling/AnnotateImageExt/issues/25</li>
               <li>Add docs/ with some catalog documentation for the built-in PixInsight 1.9.x catalogs, update NamedStars with latest IAU updates and fix bug with offset columns, add Corwin&apos;s *Galactic Globular Clusters* (2022), add OpenNGC, update Very Large Scale catalog with more objects and data</li>
               <li>Add files via upload: Update with star names added by the IAU between June, 2026 and July 16, 2026.</li>
               <li>Fix common names in NamedStars: Cleaned up the common names by removing some old duplicate name assignments, fixed the common name column offset for the last several hundred rows pointed out in issue #22, restored (removed parentheses) common names that are not actually IAU names, but are ones PixInsight included from tradition outside of the IAU names, e.g., Khan is a name from Adam Block for a star in Scorpius that was in there so I left it in.</li>
               <li>Changed alt text for GitHub banner image and Updated the alt text for the banner image in README.md.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>v1.2.2</p>
            <ul>
               <li>&quot;Name&quot; and &quot;Common name&quot; logic in the script detects whether there is a &quot;Common name&quot; column and will display it by default, as done with Messier and NGC-IC, which sometimes just results in too many duplicate names in the annotation.  I did not realize this was what was happening until today, why by default if there is a Common name column in a catalog, it will automatically be labeled under the name.  I have cleaned this up across the catalogs and just kept &quot;Common name&quot; in Messier and NGC-IC for now.</li>
               <li>Fixed inverted axisRatio values in PGCC catalog.</li>
               <li>Added 2 new external configuration properties for catalog layer configuration in catalogs-config.JSON:
  <ol><li>&quot;visible&quot;: (default false or undefined) toggles the visibilty checkbox of an enabled catalog layer</li><li>&quot;defaultSet&quot;: (default false or undefined) AnnotateImageExt will include the catalog layer in the &quot;default set&quot; with Grid, Messier, NamedStars, etc.</li></ol>
   </li>
               <li>worked on some other stuff like the Custom catalof naming problem and added some DEBUG and TODO comments</li>
               <li>cleaned up some old comments and formatting</li>
               <li>Revised README for AnnotateImageExt updates, Updated README to reflect new features, fixes, and catalog information. Changed section titles and added details about catalog layer visibility and issues fixed.</li>
               <li>Added new catalogs and updated notes on the annotation subsystem, including issues with southern hemisphere support and Vizier queries.</li>
               <li>fix missing comma in json</li>
               <li>update configs and add default=&quot;true&quot; option per catalog whether its layer is added to the default set, update field and column ordering in BFS, set Jardine enabled as a default along with Messier, NGC-IC, Calldwell and NamedStars</li>
            </ul>
            <p>v1.2</p>
            <ul>
               <li>Update catalogs-config.json and several catalog header lines and column order to align with conventions.</li>
               <li>Fixed DWB Cygnus-X position angle values, which in 1969 original catalog tables were given in galactic center offset degrees rather than equatorial degrees.  A python script quickly converts all of them. Tested in comparison to Figure 1 in DWB&apos;s 1969 paper and they look correctly aligned!  Removed gigantic, hard to visualize, Fermi Bubble structures from Very Large Scale catalog.</li>
               <li>update count of very large scale catalog in json config.</li>
               <li>add script to log git history to unordered html list</li>
            </ul>
            <p>v1.1.5</p>
            <ul>
               <li>Fix dev issue caused by extra commas in the id / name field, which was causing: &quot;*** Error: /opt/PixInsight/include/pjsr/astrometry/AstrometricMetadata.js:1815: SurfaceSplineEvaluate(): API function error (0x0001): Unknown error
return this.spline.evaluate( p );
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^&quot;</li>
               <li>Remove bak file</li>
               <li>Fix a few issues with catalogs, particularly axisRatio in DWB was incorrect, added various items to Very Large Scale catalog.</li>
               <li>Move xsgn out of the way for dev, restore backup reference of latest (1.9.4 build 1695) PixInsight NamedStars.csv</li>
               <li>add Paladini et al and Anderson et al WISE HII surveys across the galactic core.</li>
               <li>update readme and updates.xri for release, update xsgn file for main script</li>
            </ul>
            <p>v1.1</p>
            <p>Enhances PixInsight image annotation with several essential updated catalogs and flat file-based catalog and catalog layers configuration.</p>
            <ul>
               <li>Merge branch &apos;main&apos; of github.com:scottstirling/AnnotateImageExt after using the GitHub web UI to make some metadata changes in .github/.</li>
               <li>Add new catalog files and update comments in main js file</li>
               <li>Add custom layer of non-constellation asterisms such as the Big Dipper, Little Dipper, Teapot, Winter Hexagon, etc. in AsterismsLayer.js and json data for lines and labels.
        <br/>Updates and fixes to NamedStars after IAU update (fixed Sadr in wrong row, removed dups of Propus).
        <br/>Move out-of-the-box Messier.csv and NGC-IC.csv into ext/catalogs/ to be loaded like the rest of the file catalogs, and remove hard-coded loading, but keep NamedStars updated catalog in parent directory because of its *magnitudes* and customized support for it in ext/AstronomicalCatalogs.js.
        <br/>Updated catalogs-config.json with 4 new catalogs:
        <ul><li>catalogs/DWB-Cygnus_X_Region-1969-for-PixInsight.csv</li><li>catalogs/FeSt-1-Dark_Nebulae-1984-for-PixInsight.csv</li><li>catalogs/FeSt-2-Globules-1984-for-PixInsight.csv</li><li>catalogs/PGCC-Planck_Catalogue_of_Galactic_Cold_Clumps-2016-for-PixInsight.csv</li></ul>
      </li>
               <li>Add GitHub funding link for Scott Stirling</li>
               <li>update dist and code comment typo</li>
            </ul>
            <p>For more information on AnnotateImageExt, please find me on Astrobin (scottstirling) or refer to:
            <ul><li>https://github.com/scottstirling/AnnotateImageExt</li></ul>
          </p>
            <p>Copyright (c) 2026 Scott Stirling. All Rights Reserved.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
